<title>USA: Sunbeam CEO &quot;comfortable&quot; with estimates.</title>
<headline>Sunbeam CEO &quot;comfortable&quot; with estimates.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sunbeam Corp Chief Executive Officer Al Dunlap said on Tuesday he is comfortable with analysts' earnings estimates of $0.38 per share for the third quarter and $1.42 for the year.</p>
<p>&quot;We never make earnings projections other than to say we're comfortable,&quot; Dunlap told Reuters following a speech to Northeastern University College of Business alumni.</p>
<p>Dunlap reiterated his long-term goal of doubling sales to $2 billion by 1999 and growing the international business to $400 million over the same time period.</p>
<p>((Boston bureau, (617) 367-4106))</p>
